SUMMARY:JAIPUR Literature Festival:  Toronto edition
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\n{ FULL Schedule looks SUPER! }\n\nhttp
 s://tolive.com/Event-Details-Page/reference/JLF-Toronto-2026\n\nThe **Jaip
 ur Literature Festival**—held annually in the historic Pink City of Jaip
 ur\, Rajasthan—is celebrated worldwide as the **“greatest literary sho
 w on Earth.”**\n\nhttps://www.jaipurliteraturefestival.org/\n\nThere is 
 NOW---**a TORONTO edition**. 7 speakers/author interviews\n\n\\*\\*\\*Tick
 et purchase link/author bios/schedule is below.\n\nGeneral admission seati
 ng (you'll sit in the same seat all day)\n\n**DAY Pass** is $62 (for every
 thing)\n\n**INDIVIDUAL sessions**/interviews are $15 (each)\n\nhttps://tol
 ive.com/Event-Details-Page/reference/JLF-Toronto-2026?utm_medium=crossprom
 o&utm_source=partner&utm_campaign=jlf2026&utm_content=torontoisculture\n\n
 **JLF Toronto returns this September\, bringing together acclaimed writers
 \, thinkers\, artists\, and cultural leaders for a vibrant celebration of 
 literature\, ideas\, and dialogue.**\n\nJLF Toronto\, in association with 
 TO Live\, is part of the internationally renowned Jaipur Literature Festiv
 al’s global series\, produced by Teamwork Arts. The festival brings audi
 ences into conversations that travel across cultures\, disciplines\, and b
 orders\, exploring timely themes of migration\, identity\, heritage\, gend
 er\, democracy\, medicine\, and the arts.\n\n***Celebrating the richness a
 nd diversity of South Asian literary culture while embracing global perspe
 ctives***\, JLF Toronto creates a space for meaningful exchange\, fresh id
 eas\, and engaging conversations that inspire curiosity and connection.\n\
 n*Whether you're a lifelong reader\, an aspiring writer\, or simply curiou
 s about the world\, JLF Toronto invites you to discover new voices\, chall
 enge perspectives\, and join the conversation.*\n\n*Each author will speak
  for 45 minutes (on stage)*\n\n**Featured authors:**\n\n* Tanya Talaga\n* 
 John Vaillant\n* Anosh Irani\n* Vikram Vij\n* Alka Joshi\n* Martin Puchner
 \n* Dr. Nikky-Guninder Kaur Singh\n\nJoin us for an extraordinary weekend 
 where literature meets politics\, history meets imagination\, and diverse 
 voices come together to celebrate the power of words.\n\nBIO and SCHEDULE 
 here:\n\nhttps://www.tolive.com/Event-Details-Page/reference/JLF-Toronto-2
 026\n\nDAY PASS: $62 (which I have)\n\nINDIVDUAL SESSION: $15\n\n(LUNCH is
  NOT included. I plan to bring my own lunch and enjoy in at the PARK/Bercz
 y Park/Dog Fountain)\n\nSee you there! Questions?\n\n(When this event is d
 one--we head to Alliance Francaise for a concert with artists from PERU & 
 IRAN)
